    "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR completes the app-layer architecture pass on top of the `architecture-v2` branch.\n\nIt:\n- moves peer identity, encryption, verification, and stable peer-ID mapping into `PeerIdentityStore`\n- moves geohash presence, nicknames, and teleport state into `LocationPresenceStore`\n- rewires `AppRuntime`, feature models, and command handling to read through those owners instead of relying on `ChatViewModel` state bags or global channel state\n- further decomposes `ChatViewModel` into focused coordinators for public chat, private chat, Nostr, verification, media, delivery, composer, formatting, and peer identity responsibilities\n- adds focused architecture coverage for the new ownership layer and keeps the smoke harness aligned with the extracted app shell\n\n## Why\n\nThe app was still carrying too much duplicated ownership between `ChatViewModel`, feature models, and shared managers. That made state flow harder to reason about and made follow-on changes riskier than they needed to be.\n\nThis refactor makes the app-side architecture much more explicit:\n- app/runtime state has clearer owners\n- feature models consume app-layer state rather than peeking through large view-model bags\n- `ChatViewModel` is much thinner and closer to an adapter than an everything-object\n\n## Impact\n\nUser-facing behavior should stay the same, but the app layer is now:\n- easier to maintain\n- easier to test\n- safer to evolve without accidental coupling\n\nThis PR intentionally does **not** rework the transport/BLE core yet.\n\n## Validation\n\nRan:\n\n```sh\nxcodebuild -project bitchat.xcodeproj -scheme \"bitchat (macOS)\" -configuration Debug CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build\nxcodebuild -project bitchat.xcodeproj -scheme \"bitchat (iOS)\" -sdk iphonesimulator -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17' test\ngit diff --check\n```\n",
