    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Introduce typed transport events and wire ChatViewModel through the new transport event delegate while preserving the legacy delegate bridge.\n- Extract BLE outbound write backpressure into a focused buffer with priority ordering and cap trimming.\n- Tighten BLE ingress behavior for dual-role links: drop self-loopbacks, allow relayed sender IDs, preserve direct announce spoof checks, suppress duplicate ingress before the main handler, and strip padding in notification stream assembly.\n- Coalesce gossip sync requests so initial and periodic sync send one typed request instead of multiple back-to-back requests.\n\n## Why\n\nRecent runtime logs showed BLE sender spoofing warnings, unexpected notification-stream prefix drops, duplicated dual-role packet handling, and clustered gossip sync requests. The root cause was mostly dual-role BLE self-echo plus overly strict link sender binding, notification padding being treated as stream garbage, and independent sync schedules firing together.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Focused macOS tests for BLE ingress, notification stream assembly, and gossip sync coalescing: 17 tests passed.\n- `xcodebuild -project bitchat.xcodeproj -scheme \"bitchat (macOS)\" -configuration Debug CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build`\n- `xcodebuild -project bitchat.xcodeproj -scheme \"bitchat (iOS)\" -sdk iphonesimulator -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17' test`\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe next refactor should extract BLE ingress/link registry responsibilities out of `BLEService` now that the behavior has a cleaner event boundary and focused tests.",
